title: Goodryke Drafts Sweeping Amendments to the Constitution!
subtitle: Despite his extreme unpopularity, the chancellor has ordered his cabinet to begin drafting sweeping constitutional amendments.
view-if: chancellor = "Goodryke" and papen_time and papen_post_2
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/weimar_constitution.jpg

= Constitutional Amendment

As part of Goodryke’s previously announced ambition to create a “New State”—a reform of the constitution aimed at transforming the Commonwealth into a dictatorship reminiscent of the former <span class="tooltip-text" title="good mod">old Empire</span>—the continued political deadlock has led him to pursue changes to the system itself. Lacking both popular support and a parliamentary majority, it's unclear how Goodryke would institute such changes. Nonetheless, such a move would almost certainly provoke civil war—one the Commonwealth Army is in no position to easily win.

Goodryke's increasing independence and assertiveness, distancing himself from Staal's control, has alarmed the latter, who had previously sought to manipulate him. His open calls for dictatorship, along with the risks involved in keeping such an unpopular chancellor by circumventing the constitution, would unite the legions of organized labor against the government—something Staal is anxious to avoid. After all, a civil war would severely impede the Commonwealth's rearmament.